# reading 3 of euthydemus-perish.md by claude-opus-5-5
atom	wish_wise	you wish Cleinias to become wise
atom	wise_now	Cleinias is wise as yet
atom	wish_not_ignorant	you wish Cleinias not to be ignorant
atom	ignorant_now	Cleinias is now ignorant (what he is)
atom	wish_change_pred	you wish Cleinias no longer to be what he is (predicative "be": no longer to be ignorant)
atom	wish_perish	you wish Cleinias not to be (existential "be"), i.e. to perish
atom	good_friends	they are good lovers and friends of Cleinias
# The word "be" shifts sense: in S7 "no longer to be what he is" is predicative (no longer ignorant);
# in S9 it is read existentially (not to be at all, to perish). Two atoms kept apart.
P1	S2	wish_wise	kind empirical
P2	S4	¬wise_now	kind empirical
P3	S6	wish_not_ignorant	kind empirical
# Unstated: not being wise as yet, he is ignorant
A1	-	¬wise_now → ignorant_now
# S7: given he is ignorant and you wish him not ignorant, you wish him no longer to be what he is
P4	S7	ignorant_now ∧ wish_not_ignorant → wish_change_pred
C1	S7	wish_change_pred	from P2 P3 P4 A1
# S9: "which can only mean" — the sophist's equivocation from predicative to existential "be"
P5	S9	(wish_change_pred → wish_perish) | !(wish_change_pred → wish_perish)
C2	S9	wish_perish	from C1 P5
P6	S10	wish_perish → ¬good_friends	kind normative
C	S10	¬good_friends	from C2 P6
